"""The PostgreSQL adapter for ``{{ Module }}Repository``.

Rows in, entities out, at every method. Nothing above this file can hold a
live ORM instance, so the detached-instance error that shows up when a row is
serialised after its session closed is a class of bug this shape removes
rather than works around.

Composition rather than inheriting ``BaseRepository`` directly, and the reason
is concrete: the port names ``get``, ``list`` and ``delete`` too. Overriding
``get`` to return an entity would silently break ``BaseRepository.get_or_raise``,
which calls ``self.get`` and expects a row. Holding the row repository instead
also keeps this class's public surface exactly the port, so nothing above it
can reach a session through an inherited method nobody meant to expose.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

